-- Migrates HistoryDatabase v6 -> v7: the road a companion ride was on.
--
-- A route ride does not need this. Its workoutId names a course in the route
-- catalogue ("simulation:<routeId>"), and the post-ride screen, the share image
-- and the history entry all go and fetch the GPX. A companion ride has no
-- catalogue entry to fetch: the road lived in somebody else's game, and once
-- the socket closed there was nothing left of it. So a finished companion ride
-- saved as a column of numbers with no shape, which is the same ride recorded
-- worse purely because of where the road came from.
--
-- These two columns are that road travelling with the ride instead. The
-- formats are the ones the app's own route listings already use, so nothing new
-- has to know how to draw them: routeShape is a precision-5 encoded polyline
-- and routeProfile is comma-separated whole-metre elevations, evenly spaced
-- along it. app.indoorbike.shared.route.courseTrackOf puts the two back
-- together into an ordinary RouteTrack.
--
-- Empty is right for every row already in the table, and stays right for every
-- route ride and every structured workout. It reads as "no shape stored here",
-- which for a route ride means "ask the catalogue" and for a workout means
-- "there was never a road".
ALTER TABLE WorkoutSession ADD COLUMN routeShape TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '';
ALTER TABLE WorkoutSession ADD COLUMN routeProfile TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '';
